{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION TO MY OWN PRIOR COMMENT ON THIS TICKET, plus two findings that go beyond the parent's\nalready-recorded correction. 7761's plan review returned BLOCK with 7 findings; I verified the\nload-bearing ones in source before accepting them.\n\nFIRST, I WAS WRONG AND SO IS THIS TICKET'S MECHANISM SECTION. I argued (in the dependency comment\nabove) that resolve_model is \"the ONE funnel\" and that 7761 therefore owns it and blocks 172e.\nThat repeats a claim the PARENT already repudiated. eb58 comment 4 says plainly: \"My 'ONE funnel'\nkeystone claim was WRONG\", and model_classes.py:238 -- shipped by f844 -- documents \"THERE IS NO\nSINGLE INTERCEPTION POINT\". The corrected mechanism is one FUNCTION\n(model_classes.resolve_model_string, which ALREADY EXISTS) with SEPARATE CALL SITES:\n  a. config.resolve_model  -- must import model_classes LAZILY INSIDE the function body; a\n     module-level import closes a cycle, because model_classes imports config at module scope and\n     its own docstring forbids the reverse.\n  b. the batch-runner ladder expansion -- production_batch_runner.py:93\n     (cfg = dataclasses.replace(cfg, model=req.model_ladder[0])) and code_review/batch_runner.py:55.\n  c. the verifier paths -- resolve_verifier_model (verify.py:269) and _verifier_cfg\n     (plan_review/__init__.py:46), which itself has two further call sites at xcheck.py:198/336.\nTHIS TICKET'S MECHANISM SECTION STILL CARRIES THE REPUDIATED VERSION, labelled \"decided on parent\neb58 -- do not re-derive\". Six of the seven blocking findings trace to that one stale section. It\nmust be synced to eb58 comment 4.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE 7761-blocks-172e LINK I ADDED: the REASON I gave was wrong. There is no single\nfunnel that 7761 owns. What is true is narrower -- 172e (code-review's verify step) and 7761 (the\nladder) BOTH need call site (a) wired, so whichever lands first pays for it and the other consumes\nit. That is a shared-prerequisite coupling, not a strict block in one direction. Re-examine the\nlink direction rather than inheriting it from my bad reasoning.\n\nSECOND, TWO FINDINGS THAT ARE NOT COVERED BY eb58's CORRECTION -- both verified in source:\n\n1. A FOURTH LADDER SITE. workflow/runners.py:120, DefaultBatchRunner.run(), does\n   `model = req.model_ladder[0] if req.model_ladder else None` -- the identical model_ladder[0]\n   split-brain. eb58's correction enumerates the two batch runners; this third ladder consumer is\n   in nobody's scope.\n\n2. MODEL_LADDER HAS A DUAL ROLE AND THE PLAN WOULD SILENTLY BREAK HALF OF IT. MEASURED at\n   sizing.py:99-103 it is a table of (BARE_NAME, WINDOW_TOKENS) pairs:\n       (\"claude-haiku-4-5\", 200_000), (\"claude-sonnet-4-6\", 1_000_000),\n       (\"claude-opus-4-8\", 1_000_000)\n   It drives escalation ORDER via models_at_or_above (:312) AND P8's context-window budget via\n   largest_window_tokens (:137-146), which matches with `if name in model` -- a SUBSTRING test.\n   Today \"claude-sonnet-4-6\" in \"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\" is True, so qualified ids\n   work. If the ladder entries become class names, \"standard\" in \"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-\n   sonnet-4-6\" is FALSE, largest_window_tokens falls through to `return MODEL_LADDER[-1][1]` (the\n   ladder maximum) for EVERY model, and P8's budget silently changes with no error raised.\n   The plan says the rungs \"become CLASS names resolved through the same funnel\" and never\n   addresses the window-sizing half. This needs an explicit decision before implementation.\n\nNOTHING IMPLEMENTED FOR 7761. Its plan is not implementable as written."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785542780761235001,"uuid":"515de003-d746-4de8-a6d1-a380c9fd4631"}